<!--
  the mark for About: what this is, what it runs, what it was read against, and what it is under. it
  is the settings scene's toolbar button, and it is the only thing About is reached by.

  **an i in a circle rather than a heart, and the screen is what settles it.** the page credits without
  thanking - it states what this app is built on in labelled lines and spends no sentence being
  grateful at anybody - so a heart promises a register the screen behind it does not keep. what is on
  that screen is versions, terms and places to go, and this is the mark for that.

  **it is also the one mark a person is expected to recognise without a word beside it.** a section
  card carries a line saying what is behind it and a toolbar button carries a content description and a
  tooltip, so the glyph is doing work here that no icon in the section grid has to do - which is the
  argument for the convention rather than for something of our own.

  Material's own shape, at Material Symbols' 960 viewport, **with the tint it was exported carrying
  stripped**. the view tints it - `?attr/colorOnSurface` in the toolbar, as the cog on the game list is
  tinted - so a vector holding a colour of its own is one that is wrong in three of the four palettes.
  `?attr/colorControlNormal` is what the download had, and it is the same mistake the Game files folder
  arrived with.
-->
